[x] Make chezmoi apply safe on devbox =devbox-apply $Found 2026-10-10 (assistant session 13): a full apply on devbox (immutable personal-os image, headless, CHEZMOI_CONTAINER=1 to skip the paru hook) would delete the shpool user units (dot_config/systemd/exact_user removes unmanaged units), replace .bashrc with one that drops the agent-sandbox env line (. ~/.config/environment.d/50-agent-sandbox.conf) and calls fzf/luarocks/starship which are not installed, and install desktop GUI config and services (hypr, sway, waybar, rclone, otelcol). Fix: a devbox hostname block in .chezmoiignore; shpool units managed or exact_ dropped; command -v guards in .bashrc; obsidian.nvim set up only if ~/Documents/knowledge_base exists. Until then only ~/.config/nvim is applied on devbox (plus an empty knowledge_base dir as a stopgap). Also seen: Windows files (Documents/PowerShell, komorebi.json, data/windows_11_packages.json) are not ignored on Linux. UPDATE 2026-10-13 (Darrion: main is the standard branch, other branches for side work; the devbox is mine to configure): prefer a role value in chezmoi data (desktop default, agent-host here) over a hostname check, so another agent host gets the same profile. Since then: ~/.claude/skills/clearhead and ~/.pi/agent/skills/clearhead are applied here (targeted apply), and .chezmoiexternal.toml clones platform. Also review the 18 systemd units and 9 .local/bin scripts one by one; rclone holds Darrion's remotes, skip it. The branch personal-os-immutable-hooks (b54830b, 1338e50) already restricts the paru hook and rclone jobs on immutable targets: merge or reuse it.$ !2 ^2026-10-10T17:41 %2026-10-13T17:16 #01a126e8-3e55-7a51-8b1f-2a595c129918
